      "message": "Confirmed: VPP intentionally builds static rdma-core with ENABLE_RESOLVE_NEIGH\u003d0 to avoid the libnl dependency, so ibv_get_device_index() returns -1. Keeping the device-index fallback is therefore reasonable.\n\nCould we nevertheless simplify the netlink implementation by using one parameterized multipart-dump lookup helper? Both lookups perform the same request construction, sequence filtering, NLMSG_ERROR/NLMSG_DONE handling, attribute matching, and u32 extraction. The call site would reduce to DEV_NAME -\u003e DEV_INDEX, then NDEV_INDEX -\u003e PORT_INDEX filtered by DEV_INDEX. This preserves the required fallback while removing the separate send functions and duplicated receive/parsing loops.",
